Why it works: the native details/summary element is a browser-built disclosure widget — toggling open/closed is built in, so zero JS is needed and it is keyboard accessible out of the box (Enter/Space toggle, Tab through links). The menu list is positioned absolutely relative to details so it overlays content instead of pushing it down. Removing the default marker with list-style plus the -webkit-details-marker rule keeps the trigger looking like a button. Bonus: clicking outside does not close it; if you need that behavior, one two-line click handler on document is the only JS you would add.

